This directory contains support software related to 3PL.

The makefile contained in each directory usually just installs
the associated file or files in an installation directory,
~/install/3pl in sub-directories bin, lib, include or src as
appropriate.

Executable scripts, bin2c, bin2py, edif2bit, info2c and info2py,
are installed in ~/install/3pl/bin and can be executed on any
host computer.

C source files must be compiled for the computer on which they
will be executed, be it a workstation or a Zynq ARM CPU.

Python3 import files are imported directly into python application
code on the target platform.

In the special case of fpga_py_extension.c this python C extension
code must be installed using setup.py in the python library of
the computer on which the python application code is to execute.




bin2c
-----
    bin2c               TCL script
    
    target FPGA         any
    app language        C
    install             ~/install/3pl/bin
    
    Convert a Xilinx .bit FPGA configuration file to a C include file
    so that the configuration data can be incorporated into a C
    application program. The configuration can then be loaded into
    the FPGA by the application program without need for a separate
    configuration file.

bin2py
------
    bin2py              Python script
    
    target FPGA         any
    app language        Python3
    install             ~/install/3pl/bin
    
    Convert a Xilinx .bit FPGA configuration file to a Python3 module
    so that the configuration data can be incorporated into a Python3
    application program. The configuration can then be loaded into
    the FPGA by the application program without need for a separate
    configuration file.
    
    
edif2bit
--------
    edif2bit            shell script
    
    target FPGA         any
    app language        any
    install             ~/install/3pl/bin
    
    Place and route a Xilinx EDIF netlist file using either ISE
    or Vivado (default). A bitfile is produced.

    Various shell scripts and TCL source files.
    
    Sources for edif2bit shell script.

info2py
-------
    info2py.py          Python3 module
    
    target FPGA         zynq or any with CPU-FPGA serial link
    app language        Python3
    install             ~/install/3pl/include
    
    Process a 3PL .info JSON structure to produce Python interface functions
    between a CPU and 3PL code in an FPGA. In the case of FPGA boards
    with a serial communication interface, e.g. Gadget Factory Papilio,
    data transfers will be via the serial link. For Zynq platforms data
    transfers will be via the AXI buses.
    
    info2py.py is imported into the application python program. It reads
    the interface information either from a design.info file
    (info_from_file()) or from the identical text obtainable from the
    loaded FPGA configuration (info_from_fpga()). From this it creates an
    internal Python module containing the FPGA interface functions.

    
    info2py             shell script calling info2py.py directly
    
    target FPGA         zynq or any with CPU-FPGA serial link
    app language        Python3
    install             ~/install/3pl/bin
    
    This script calls info2py.py as __main__ and creates a Python
    module file 'design_fpga.py' which can be imported into the CPU
    Python application program. This module defines the ARM CPU functions
    to communicate with the FPGA 3PL application code.
    

serial
------
    Communication between CPU and FPGA via serial link.

    cpu_serial
    ----------
        cpu_serial.py       Python3 module
    
        target FPGA         any with CPU-FPGA serial link
        app language        Python3
            
        Python3 CPU/FPGA interface functions.
    
    uart_cpu
    --------
        cpu_serial.h, cpu_serial.o
    
        target FPGA         any with CPU-FPGA serial link
        app language        C
            
        C CPU/FPGA interface functions.
    
    uart_info2c
    -----------
        uart_info2c         Python3 script
    
        target FPGA         any with CPU-FPGA serial link
        app language        Python3
            
        Create C CPU/FPGA interface functions.

zynq
----
    Communication between Zynq ARM CPU and FPGA via AXI bus.
   
    fpga
    ----
        fpga.c, fpga.h      C source
    
        target FPGA         Zynq
        app language        C
            
        C CPU/FPGA interface functions.

        
        fpga.py             Python3 module
    
        target FPGA         Zynq
        app language        Python3
            
        Python CPU/FPGA interface functions.
       

    info2c
    ------
        info2c              Python3 module
    
        target FPGA         Zynq
        app language        C
            
        Process a 3PL .info JSON structure to produce a C .h include file
        defining interface functions between the Zynq ARM CPU and
        3PL code in the FPGA. Data transfers are via the AXI buses.
    
    lib_py_ext
    ----------
    
        fpga_read_write.c   C source
    
        target FPGA         Zynq
        app language        Python3
            
        Python C extension functions for low-level AXI bus data transfers.
        Uses fpga/fpga.c and fpga/fpga.h.
        
        setup.py
        --------
    
        target FPGA         zynq or any with CPU-FPGA serial link
        app language        Python3
            
        A minimal Python3 program to install C extension module
        fpga_read_write linked with fpga.c above.



